.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fBAdwToggleGroup\fR / \fBAdwViewSwitcher\fR: exclusive, linked segments.
.PP
It respects the space it is given: with \fBwidth\fR\fB(Fill)\fR (or when a stacked row asks for 100%) the segments stretch evenly with no dead space; when too wide it shrinks fairly and never overshoots its limits.
.SH FUNCTIONS
.TP
.B toggle_group(items: Vec<ToggleItem<'a, T, M>>, active: Option<T>, on_select: impl Fn(T) \-> M + 'a)
Builds a \fBToggleGroup\fR.
.SH PROPERTIES
Builder methods, chained after the constructor.
.TP
.B \&.metrics(m: Metrics)
.TP
.B \&.homogeneous(h: bool)
All segments the same width (\fBAdwToggleGroup:homogeneous\fR).
.TP
.B \&.window_width(width: f32)
Follows the window's mode: in mobile mode (\fBwindow::is_mobile(width)\fR, the \fB[windows]\fR mobile\-max\-width\fB breakpoint) every segment that has an icon *and* a label shows the icon\fR only; above it, icon and text. A segment with no icon has nothing shorter to show and falls back to its text. Same rule as \fBMenuPresentation::resolve\fR.
.TP
.B \&.compact(compact: Option<bool>)
Icons or full content for the segments that have both, all together. Prefer \fBwindow_width\fR; this takes the decision directly. Without either (\fBNone\fR) the group falls back to the space: icons as soon as any segment would be squeezed.
.TP
.B \&.width(w: impl Into<Length>)
\fBLength::Fill\fR makes the group fill the available width, each segment taking an equal share (\fBflex: 1\fR) with its content centered.
